  "_note": "Every sound in the game (M7 feel, crates/core/src/sound.rs). The core synthesises each voice from its layers once, when the page first asks (after the reader's first click), and says each frame which voices to play, how loud, how fast and where; the page only plays them (web/sound.js). A new sound is one row here and one sound::cue(w, \"name\", …) in the core. Layer fields: wave (sine, tri, square, saw, noise, crackle), hz [from, to] swept straight over the layer, at_ms and ms (when the layer starts and how long it lasts; ms 0 is to the voice's end), attack_ms, decay_ms (the time for the level to fall to about a third; 0 holds it), gain_pct, lp_hz and hp_hz [from, to] one-pole filters (0 is none), bp_hz [from, to] with bp_q_pct (a resonant band), am_mhz and am_pct (a swell, millihertz), vib_mhz and vib_pct (a wobble in pitch), density (clicks a second, for crackle). A voice: ms long, peak_pct (its loudest sample after it is made, percent of full scale), level_pct (how loud it plays), bus, gap_ticks (the same voice is not started again sooner), near_m and reach_m (full level within near_m, falling as near_m / distance, gone at reach_m; reach_m 0 is heard everywhere, not placed), loop (played round and round; its level comes from the core every frame).",
